# Agent provider secrets — server-side ONLY.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in a key for whichever provider you're testing.
# Never use a client-exposed prefix (VITE_ / NEXT_PUBLIC_): these are read by
# server code only. `.env` is gitignored; this example file is safe to commit.
#
# Only `bun run scripts/dev-real.ts` (this repo's local smoke test) reads these.
# The registry reads none of them, and the published CLI generates no provider
# code and installs no adapter — which model a project runs on is decided in its
# own `agent-model.ts`, and the key is loaded by that adapter from the project's
# own environment. The `--provider` flag below is dev-real.ts's; `init` has none.

# Google Gemini (default for the local smoke test).
# The @ai-sdk/google adapter reads GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY on its own;
# the smoke-test launcher also accepts GEMINI_API_KEY / GOOGLE_API_KEY.
#GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# OpenAI — `bun run scripts/dev-real.ts --provider openai`.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Anthropic (Claude) — `bun run scripts/dev-real.ts --provider anthropic`.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
